WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.702
Start and controls
Take a seat and press Ready. The host starts when everyone is ready. Your cards or dice are at the bottom.

00:00:12.702 --> 00:00:19.002
Follow the turn prompt. Wait for animations to finish; an expired turn is played automatically. Use Return to room after settlement.

00:00:19.002 --> 00:00:35.002
Sevens: minimize covered-card penalties
Each player has 13 cards. Follow the spade-seven holder in a match with Dragon Slaying enabled and aim for the lowest covered-card penalty.

00:00:35.002 --> 00:00:46.002
Open with the spade seven
Click the spade seven to play it directly. Then open another suit with its seven or extend an open end with the adjacent rank of that suit.

00:00:46.002 --> 00:00:55.002
Turns run counterclockwise. Each row extends from 7 down to A and up to K without gaps or wrapping.

00:00:55.002 --> 00:01:04.902
Play whenever you can
Watch other players extend rows or cover a card when blocked. Only the number of their covered cards is visible.

00:01:04.902 --> 00:01:13.002
Any legal play prevents covering. Only a player with no legal play must choose a card to cover.

00:01:13.002 --> 00:01:33.002
Build each suit outward
Speed through the growing rows. On your turn, clicking an available legal hand card sends it directly.

00:01:33.002 --> 00:01:45.102
Confirm a covered card
You now have no legal extension. Click the card to cover, then press the confirmation showing its name and penalty; cancel lets you choose again.

00:01:45.102 --> 00:01:55.002
Covered cards score penalties: A=1, 2–10 face value, J=11, Q=12, K=13.

00:01:55.002 --> 00:02:08.202
Dragon Slaying closes both ends
Watch the following public plays and suit closure. With Dragon Slaying enabled, playing an A or K closes both ends of that suit.

00:02:08.202 --> 00:02:19.002
Other suits remain open. If all four close, the game automatically covers every remaining card. With this option off, rows can continue to both A and K.

00:02:19.002 --> 00:02:47.001
Speed through the remaining cards
All further plays and covers run in order at higher speed. Watch dimmed suits, hand counts, and your covered-card penalty.

00:02:47.001 --> 00:03:03.001
Finish the last few turns
Resolve the remaining hand cards. Once every card is played or covered, the game reveals covers and calculates penalties.

00:03:03.001 --> 00:03:20.000
Sevens: lower penalties win
Demo S wins with 11 points. Demo E has 12, N has 17, and W has 28.
